  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Girijesh Kumar Dubey vs Principal Secy. Deptt. Food Safety And ... on 19 September, 2024 Author: Rajesh Singh Chauhan Bench: Rajesh Singh Chauhan High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:64754 Court No. - 4 Case :- Writ - A No. - 8014 of 2024 Petitioner :- Girijesh Kumar Dubey Respondent :- Principal Secy. Deptt. Food Safety And Drug Administration Lko. And 2 Othe Counsel for Petitioner :- Manoj Kumar Yadav,Rita Yadav Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C. Hon'ble Rajesh Singh Chauhan,J. 1. Heard Sri Manoj Kumar Yadav, learned counsel for the petitioner and Sri Jyotendra Verma, learned Standing Counsel. 2.",
    "facts": "By means of this petition, the petitioner has prayed the following relief:- \"(i) Issue a Writ, or der or direction in the nature of Certiorari thereby quashing the letter No. 1/733013/2024-88-2001 (003)/4/2024 dated 5 September 2024 issued by opp. Party No.1 i.e. Principal Secretary, Department Food, Safety and Drug Administration by which he suspended to the petitioner contained as Annexure No. 1 Girijesh Kumar Dubey vs Principal Secy. Deptt. Food Safety And ... on 19 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/120144481/ 1 to this writ petition in the interest of justice. (ii) Issue a Writ, order or direction in the nature of Mandamus thereby commanding to the opp. Party No. 3 i.e inquiry officers/ Assistant Commissioner (Food) Prayagraj Mandal Prayagraj conclude the inquiry fair and proper within a stipulated period fixed by this Hon'ble court.\" 3. By means of this petition, the petitioner has challenged the suspension order dated 05.09.2024 and also prayed that a direction may be issued to the enquiry officer to conduct and conclude the departmental enquiry with expedition, strictly in accordance with law. 4.",
    "arguments": "The counsel for the petitioner has stated that no charge-sheet has been provided to the petitioner till date. 5. The learned Standing Counsel has no instruction as to whether the charge-sheet has been provided to the petitioner or not."
  },
